  clock: 2  # c58a
  nonce: c58a  # c58a
  set:  # c58a
    fields:  # c58a
      root_cause: "ERLANG/ELIXIR HALF: LOCALIZED TO A LINE, 2026-09-04. Not an arity collapse in the symbol table -- both analyzers mint one symbol per name/arity with correct spans. The defect is in the ENCLOSING-FUNCTION LOOKUP that anchors an edge to its caller. _get_enclosing_function_erlang (hypergumbo-lang-common/erlang.py:441-459) walks up the parent chain, reaches the fun_decl node, and then discards that structural knowledge: it takes only the function's atom (the BASE name) and does local_symbols.get(base_name). ErlangAnalyzer.register_symbol writes global_symbols[base_name] = symbol for every arity, so the bare name resolves to whichever arity registered LAST in file order. elixir.py:272-289 has the same shape (_get_function_name then a bare local_symbols lookup) and reproduces identically. In both cases the correct span was already in hand at the enclosing declaration node. GO/DIRECTION HALF: not this mechanism -- see the 2026-09-04 discussion entry; it is the sink_before_source shape, owned and addressed by INV-muhij."  # c58a
  add:  # c58a
    tags: [erlang, elixir]  # c58a
- op: discuss  # 9edf
  at: '2026-09-04T17:55:40Z'  # 9edf
  by: agent  # 9edf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9edf
  clock: 3  # 9edf
  nonce: 9edf  # 9edf
  message: "FIRST VERIFICATION PASS ON THIS ITEM, 2026-09-04, dev ef9c55f8bf. Filed 2026-09-03 with no discussion; both instances re-derived at tip rather than read off the filing. The two instances turn out to have DIFFERENT owners, so they are reported separately.\n\nINSTANCE 1 (ERLANG, ANCHORING) -- REPRODUCES, AND THE ROOT CAUSE IS NOW A LINE.\n\nThe filed evidence re-read at source: rabbitmq deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_channel.erl really does define get_consumer_timeout/0 at 818, whose body calls application:get_env at 819, and get_consumer_timeout/2 at 2743-2744, which is a pure forwarding wrapper (its whole body is get_queue_consumer_timeout(PA, State)). The filing is accurate.\n\nMinimal fixture, production ErlangAnalyzer, one file, three functions:\n\n    get_timeout/0   span 4-6    body calls application:get_env at line 5\n    other/0         span 8-9\n    get_timeout/2   span 11-12  body calls get_timeout() at line 12\n\n    EDGE EMITTED:  line=5  src=erlang:mod.erl:11-12:get_timeout/2:function\n                           dst=erlang:application:0-0:get_env:function\n\nThe source call on line 5 is anchored to a symbol spanning lines 11-12. That is this item's statement violated, minimally and at tip. The symbols themselves are correct -- both arities exist with the right spans -- so this is not the arity collapse the filing guessed at; see the rewritten root_cause for the line.\n\nA SECOND SYMPTOM OF THE SAME LOOKUP, filed here rather than chased: the local call get_timeout() at line 12 (arity 0) resolves to get_timeout/2, a self-loop. Wrong CALLEE, where the above is a wrong ANCHOR. Same base-name key, opposite end of the edge.\n\nELIXIR CHECKED -- the item's own last line says \"Erlang arity collapse should be checked against elixir\". Done, and it reproduces:\n\n    System.get_env at line 3, inside Mod.get_timeout/0 (span 2-4)\n    EDGE EMITTED:  src=elixir:mod.ex:10-12:Mod.get_timeout:function   <- the arity-2 clause\n\nElixir is worse in one respect: its symbol NAMES carry no arity at all (both are Mod.get_timeout), so the two clauses are distinguishable only by span, and every local call to an overloaded name fans out an edge to each arity.\n\nINSTANCE 2 (GO, DIRECTION) -- NOT THIS ITEM'S MECHANISM, AND ADDRESSED ELSEWHERE TODAY.\n\nThe filing groups it under \"the symbol a source is anchored to does not contain the source call\", but the gocryptfs defect is not containment -- both calls ARE inside callFidoCommand. It is ORDERING: the sink at :61 precedes the source at :65, so the asserted intra-procedural route cannot execute. That is exactly INV-muhij's statement, which named the same gocryptfs row, and INV-muhij was satisfied today in PR #774: gocryptfs UI-FS moved violated(n=1) -> inconclusive(n=1) on the production path with the row still reported and a sink_before_source_only caveat raised. So the consequence the filing cared about -- a false verdict resting on this row alone -- is discharged. NOT discharged, and left with INV-muhij's own open question rather than duplicated here: the row still reports hops=0, still asserts the impossible route, and the rule is broader than ideal because the DDG exposes no loop spans at that decision point.\n\nSTATUS: stays violated, P1, on instance 1 alone. It is a real, reproducible, two-language anchoring defect with a one-line root cause and no owner. The go half should be read as cross-referenced to INV-muhij, not as this item's residual.\n\nNOT DONE: no fix written; the wrong-callee symptom is not sized; languages other than erlang and elixir are unswept for the enclosing-lookup shape (the pattern to grep for is an enclosing-declaration walk that ends in a bare-name dictionary lookup)."  # 9edf
