- op: discuss  # 9bbd
  at: '2026-09-23T06:39:01Z'  # 9bbd
  by: agent  # 9bbd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9bbd
  clock: 5  # 9bbd
  nonce: 9bbd  # 9bbd
  message: "SATISFIED ON THE FILED INSTANCE (erlang), and on elixir, which the row asked to check. Fixed in PR #1147 (6196148d11 + 5085454e1d). THE GENERAL STATEMENT IS NOT ASSERTED: other analyzers still violate it; filed as a separate row (see below). The go half was already owned by INV-muhij (see 09-04 entry).\n\nFILED REPRO RE-RUN (production analyzer, rabbitmq deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_channel.erl, dev pinned at 9aac6ffe8d in a worktree vs this fix):\n  dev:   line 819 application:get_env -> src get_consumer_timeout/2 [2743-2744]  contains=False\n  fixed: line 819 application:get_env -> src get_consumer_timeout/0 [818-824]    contains=True\n  (a second one in the same file: line 806 moved from format_state/2 [808-814] to format_state/1 [805-806])\n\nPRODUCTION PATH (verify-claims --claims docs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml --format json on rabbitmq deps/rabbit, both arms): all 7 claim verdicts unchanged. The dev arm's host-secret-no-logging evidence path starts at get_consumer_timeout/2:2743-2744; the fixed arm has no path starting at get_consumer_timeout at all. So the finding at this row's filed id (rabbitmq:host-secret-no-logging:17, labelled TP by both of 0012's blind adjudicators) is GONE. That is the fix working: both adjudicators' real chain runs through a record field (#conf.consumer_timeout at :483), which the walk does not follow; the tool reached the finding only through the mis-anchor, then 13 hops through rabbit_khepri to an unrelated logger call. Anchored correctly, get_consumer_timeout/0 has no path to a logging sink. Recall the tool never had, not recall this change lost.\n\nROOT CAUSE, as fixed: (1) erlang keyed the enclosing lookup on the bare atom -> now name/arity off the fun_decl, choosing the candidate whose span contains it (-ifdef/-else); (2) elixir keyed on the short name -> now the position of the enclosing def node; a symbol-less (quoted, INV-sinah) def is walked past to its macro; (3) Pass 2 received only symbol_by_name (one symbol per name), so ejabberd's -ifdef copy of json_encode/1 never reached edge extraction -> TreeSitterAnalyzer.file_symbols() now hands Pass 2 the full list. Alongside: an erlang local call resolves by arity (get_timeout() inside /2 had been a self-loop); an elixir def head is no longer a call.\n\nMEASURED (instrument ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mozas_09222026/anchor_probe.py + compare.py + vanished.py; cowboy, rebar3, recon, ejabberd, phoenix, plausible, livebook): calls outside their src span, erlang 1,306 -> 0 of 44,449; elixir 7,166 -> 0 of 26,744. Every call site lost is accounted for: 1,551 def heads, 1 quoted def head, 1 dedup merge onto an identical (src,dst) edge. Seeded samples of gained and lost edges were read at source: all correct. Mutation-checked: name/arity key, span containment for -ifdef, file_symbols (the -ifdef test goes red without it), def-head skip, guard branch.\n\nA TEST OF MINE WAS VACUOUS AT FIRST AND I CAUGHT IT: the first -ifdef fixture put the two alternatives adjacent, so they coalesced into one symbol and the test could not reach the defect. Rewritten with a function between them (ejabberd's misc.erl shape); it now fails without the fix."  # 9bbd
